source: crates/daemon/tests/cli_help.rs
expression: stdout
---
Reply later, or wait for a reply, until a time.

When they wrote last: reply later. The conversation leaves the desk and the reply queue and comes back to both at the time. When you wrote last: it leaves Waiting on and comes back at the time if nobody has replied, joining the reply queue. Prints an undo id for `mxr undo`.

Usage: mxr desk later [OPTIONS] --at <AT> <THREAD_IDS>...

Arguments:
  <THREAD_IDS>...
          Thread ids, as `mxr desk --format ids` prints them

Options:
      --at <AT>
          When it comes back, in local time: `tue 9`, `tomorrow`, `in 3d`, `next week`, or RFC3339. Preview with `mxr time`

      --dry-run
          Show what would be set without changing anything

      --format <FORMAT>
          [possible values: table, json, jsonl, csv, ids]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
